   "t": 1172,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/pp2pppp/2n2n2/1Npp4/3P1B2/4P3/PPP2PPP/R2QKBNR b KQkq - 2 5",
   "line": [
    "Nb5"
   ],
   "spoken": "And the trap springs — a knight to b5, with the threat of a fork on c7 that has no good answer short of an awkward king move. This is exactly why the Jobava is so appealing: strong players walk right into it.",
   "kind": "tactic"
  },
