   "fen": "r3kb1r/1p3p1p/p1n1bp2/2pB4/5B2/2P1P3/P1P2PPP/2KR2NR b - - 3 13",
   "line": [
    "Bd5"
   ],
   "spoken": "Don't capture the bishop, which would only mend the opponent's pawn structure — the right idea is to meet it centrally on d5, supported by a pawn if it's attacked. The awkward-looking retreat would trap the bishop, so it's the right concept but the wrong execution.",
   "kind": "plan"
  },
  {
