   "line": [
    "Nc6"
   ],
   "spoken": "The discipline that would have avoided the mistake: every single time you move a pawn, spend a few seconds asking which squares you've just given up and whether the opponent can occupy them. At this level that habit is what separates good moves from careless ones.",
   "kind": "plan"
  },
  {
